---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Humans of PSG"
  description="Humans of PSG turns memories into meaningful stories that strengthen the global PSG network — through Memories, Moments, Movements, Models, and Milestones."
>
  <div class="wrap story-body">
    <p class="section-title">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Humans of PSG</h1>
    <p>
      Humans of PSG (HOP) is a digital platform that captures authentic, first-person stories from the
      PSG community &mdash; alumni, students, faculty, and friends &mdash; to inspire learning, mentorship,
      collaboration, and lifelong connections. Our mission: turn memories into meaningful stories that
      strengthen the global PSG network.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every story is told in the subject's own words, alongside a portrait, and contributed by
      volunteers and alumni who take the time to sit down, listen, and write.
    </p>

    <h2>The 5M Framework</h2>
    <p>
      The Alumni Journey is organized around five pillars &mdash; from memories to milestones, each with
      its own home and its own way of contributing.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Memories</strong> &mdash; hosted on Substack (by Authors &amp; Admins). Collaborative
        storytelling with alumni and authors worldwide to preserve and share lasting memories.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Moments</strong> &mdash; hosted on LinkedIn (by Mentors &amp; Admins). Highlights of
        current achievements, live updates, and opportunities, connecting those who need support with
        those who can help.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Movements</strong> &mdash; run through Mentorship (Wellpin &amp; the HOP Mentor WhatsApp
        team). Meaningful mentor&ndash;mentee connections that create long-term value through guidance,
        support, and a spirit of giving back.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Models</strong> &mdash; the HOP Learning Website. Mental models such as the Learning
        Pyramid, Eisenhower Matrix, and Pareto Principle, to help alumni learn, unlearn, and relearn.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Milestones</strong> &mdash; this site's Content Management System, managed by HOP Global
        Admins with content drafted and contributed by alumni through their own login accounts. It
        archives the complete Humans of PSG journey, making stories and contributions accessible to
        alumni and the wider public.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      This site &mdash; the Stories, Memories, Moments, Movements, Models, and Milestones pages you're
      browsing now &mdash; is that archive: the Milestones CMS layer of the wider 5M ecosystem.
    </p>

    <p>
      Want to contribute a story? See the project's
      <a href="https://github.com/tech-itrace/humansofpsg">
        GitHub repository
      </a>
      for how to submit one.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
